"本文面向已经会写 Triton kernel、也了解社区版 `triton.autotune` 基本概念的用户，重点说明 Triton-Ascend "
"的推荐用法："
msgstr ""
"This article is intended for users who already know how to write Triton "
"kernels and are familiar with the basic concepts of the community version of"
" `triton.autotune`, with a focus on explaining the recommended usage of "
"Triton-Ascend:"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:7
msgid "Triton-Ascend 上的推荐 autotune 写法；"
msgstr "Recommended autotune practices on Triton-Ascend."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:8
msgid "`configs=[]` 在 Ascend 后端中的含义；"
msgstr "The meaning of `configs=[]` in the Ascend backend;"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:9
msgid "自动 Tiling 模式的适用边界，以及何时回到手写 `triton.Config`。"
msgstr ""
"Applicable boundaries of the automatic Tiling mode, and when to return to "
"handwritten `triton.Config`."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:11
msgid "快速上手"
msgstr "Quick Start"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:13
msgid ""
"在 Triton-Ascend 上，推荐保留社区版 `@triton.autotune` 的基本写法；当希望系统自动生成并评估候选配置时，将 "
"`configs` 设为 `[]`："
msgstr ""
"On Triton-Ascend, it is recommended to keep the basic usage of the community"
" version `@triton.autotune`; when you want the system to automatically "
"generate and evaluate candidate configurations, set `configs` to `[]`:"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:15
msgid ""
"\"\"\"\n"
"Vector Add\n"
"=============\n"
"\"\"\"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"import torch\n"
"import torch_npu\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"import triton.backends.ascend.runtime\n"
"from triton.backends.ascend.testing import do_bench_npu\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@triton.autotune(configs=[], key=[\"n_elements\"])\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def add_kernel(x_ptr,  # *Pointer* to first input vector.\n"
"               y_ptr,  # *Pointer* to second input vector.\n"
"               output_ptr,  # *Pointer* to output vector.\n"
"               n_elements,  # Size of the vector.\n"
"               BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,  # Number of elements each program should process.\n"
"               # NOTE: `constexpr` so it can be used as a shape value.\n"
"               ):\n"
"    # There are multiple 'programs' processing different data. We identify which program\n"
"    # we are here:\n"
"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)  # We use a 1D launch grid so axis is 0.\n"
"    # This program will process inputs that are offset from the initial data.\n"
"    # For instance, if you had a vector of length 256 and block_size of 64, the programs\n"
"    # would each access the elements [0:64, 64:128, 128:192, 192:256].\n"
"    # Note that offsets is a list of pointers:\n"
"    block_start = pid * BLOCK_SIZE\n"
"    offsets = block_start + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n"
"    # Create a mask to guard memory operations against out-of-bounds accesses.\n"
"    mask = offsets < n_elements\n"
"    # Load x and y from DRAM, masking out any extra elements in case the input is not a\n"
"    # multiple of the block size.\n"
"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n"
"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n"
"    output = x + y\n"
"    # Write x + y back to DRAM.\n"
"    tl.store(output_ptr + offsets, output, mask=mask)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def add_torch(x, y):\n"
"    return x + y\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def add_autotune(x, y):\n"
"    output = torch.empty_like(x)\n"
"    n_elements = output.numel()\n"
"    add_kernel[lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n_elements, meta[\"BLOCK_SIZE\"]), )](x, y, output, n_elements)\n"
"    return output\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def test_add(size: int):\n"
"    x = torch.rand(size, device=\"npu\")\n"
"    y = torch.rand(size, device=\"npu\")\n"
"\n"
"    output_torch = add_torch(x, y)\n"
"    output_triton = add_autotune(x, y)\n"
"    assert torch.allclose(output_triton, output_torch)\n"
"    print(f\"Vector Add {size} PASSED!\")\n"
"    triton_us = do_bench_npu(lambda: add_autotune(x, y))\n"
"    torch_us = do_bench_npu(lambda: add_torch(x, y))\n"
"    print(f\"Triton kernel execution time: {triton_us:.4f} ms\")\n"
"    print(f\"PyTorch kernel execution time: {torch_us:.4f} ms\")\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n"
"    test_add(98432)"
msgstr ""
"\"\"\"\n"
"Vector Add\n"
"=============\n"
"\"\"\"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"import torch\n"
"import torch_npu\n"
"import triton\n"
"import triton.language as tl\n"
"import triton.backends.ascend.runtime\n"
"from triton.backends.ascend.testing import do_bench_npu\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@triton.autotune(configs=[], key=[\"n_elements\"])\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def add_kernel(x_ptr,  # *Pointer* to first input vector.\n"
"               y_ptr,  # *Pointer* to second input vector.\n"
"               output_ptr,  # *Pointer* to output vector.\n"
"               n_elements,  # Size of the vector.\n"
"               BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,  # Number of elements each program should process.\n"
"               # NOTE: `constexpr` so it can be used as a shape value.\n"
"               ):\n"
"    # There are multiple 'programs' processing different data. We identify which program\n"
"    # we are here:\n"
"    pid = tl.program_id(axis=0)  # We use a 1D launch grid so axis is 0.\n"
"    # This program will process inputs that are offset from the initial data.\n"
"    # For instance, if you had a vector of length 256 and block_size of 64, the programs\n"
"    # would each access the elements [0:64, 64:128, 128:192, 192:256].\n"
"    # Note that offsets is a list of pointers:\n"
"    block_start = pid * BLOCK_SIZE\n"
"    offsets = block_start + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n"
"    # Create a mask to guard memory operations against out-of-bounds accesses.\n"
"    mask = offsets < n_elements\n"
"    # Load x and y from DRAM, masking out any extra elements in case the input is not a\n"
"    # multiple of the block size.\n"
"    x = tl.load(x_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n"
"    y = tl.load(y_ptr + offsets, mask=mask)\n"
"    output = x + y\n"
"    # Write x + y back to DRAM.\n"
"    tl.store(output_ptr + offsets, output, mask=mask)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def add_torch(x, y):\n"
"    return x + y\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def add_autotune(x, y):\n"
"    output = torch.empty_like(x)\n"
"    n_elements = output.numel()\n"
"    add_kernel[lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(n_elements, meta[\"BLOCK_SIZE\"]), )](x, y, output, n_elements)\n"
"    return output\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def test_add(size: int):\n"
"    x = torch.rand(size, device=\"npu\")\n"
"    y = torch.rand(size, device=\"npu\")\n"
"\n"
"    output_torch = add_torch(x, y)\n"
"    output_triton = add_autotune(x, y)\n"
"    assert torch.allclose(output_triton, output_torch)\n"
"    print(f\"Vector Add {size} PASSED!\")\n"
"    triton_us = do_bench_npu(lambda: add_autotune(x, y))\n"
"    torch_us = do_bench_npu(lambda: add_torch(x, y))\n"
"    print(f\"Triton kernel execution time: {triton_us:.4f} ms\")\n"
"    print(f\"PyTorch kernel execution time: {torch_us:.4f} ms\")\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n"
"    test_add(98432)"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:88
msgid "这表示："
msgstr "This indicates:"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:90
msgid "`key` 的语义与社区版保持一致，用于决定哪些输入变化会触发重新选择配置；"
msgstr ""
"The semantics of `key` remain consistent with the community edition, used to"
" determine which input changes will trigger re-selection of configuration."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:91
msgid ""
"`configs=[]` 在 Triton-Ascend 中表示“由 Ascend backend "
"自动生成候选配置并完成寻优”，而不是“没有可选配置”。"
msgstr ""
"`configs=[]` in Triton-Ascend means \"the Ascend backend automatically "
"generates candidate configurations and completes the optimization search,\" "
"rather than \"no available configurations.\""

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:93
msgid "1. 先启用 Ascend 对 autotune 的扩展"
msgstr "1\\. First enable Ascend's extension for autotune."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:95
msgid "只有导入下面这行后，才会进入 Triton-Ascend 的 autotune 扩展路径："
msgstr ""
"Only after importing the following line will the autotune extension path of "
"Triton-Ascend be entered:"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:97
msgid "import triton.backends.ascend.runtime\n"
msgstr "import triton.backends.ascend.runtime\n"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:101
msgid ""
"如果没有这一步，使用的仍然是社区版 `triton.autotune`，`configs=[]` 也不会触发 Ascend 的自动 Tiling 生成。"
msgstr ""
"If this step is not performed, the community version of `triton.autotune` is"
" still used, and `configs=[]` will not trigger Ascend's automatic Tiling "
"generation."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:103
msgid "2. `@triton.autotune` 必须直接包在 `@triton.jit` 外层"
msgstr ""
"2\\. `@triton.autotune` must be wrapped directly around the outside of "
"`@triton.jit`."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:105
msgid "必须写成下面这种顺序："
msgstr "Must be written in the following order:"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:107
msgid ""
"@triton.autotune(configs=[], key=[\"M\", \"N\"])\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def kernel(...):\n"
"    ...\n"
msgstr ""
"@triton.autotune(configs=[], key=[\"M\", \"N\"])\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def kernel(...):\n"
"    ...\n"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:114
msgid ""
"`@triton.autotune` 必须直接包在 `@triton.jit` 外层，不能在两者之间插入其他 decorator。否则会导致无法对 "
"kernel DSL 进行解析，从而无法进入 Triton-Ascend 的自动 Tiling 生成与寻优链路。"
msgstr ""
"`@triton.autotune` must be directly wrapped around `@triton.jit`, and no "
"other decorators should be inserted between them. Otherwise, the kernel DSL "
"cannot be parsed, and the automatic Tiling generation and optimization "
"pipeline of Triton-Ascend cannot be entered."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:116
msgid "3. `key` 的含义与社区一致"
msgstr "3\\. The meaning of `key` is consistent with the community."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:118
msgid ""
"`key` 的本质是 autotune 的 cache key。凡是填入 `key` 的参数，只要取值发生变化，就会触发重新 autotune。"
msgstr ""
"The essence of `key` is the cache key for autotune. Any parameter filled "
"into `key` will trigger re-autotuning whenever its value changes."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:120
msgid ""
"大多数情况下，`key` 里放的是 `M/N/K`、`seq_len`、`hidden_size` 这类 shape 参数，因为它们往往会显著影响最优 "
"Tiling；但 `key` 并不只限于 shape 参数，只要某个参数变化会影响配置选择，也可以放入 `key`。"
msgstr ""
"In most cases, the `key` contains shape parameters such as `M/N/K`, "
"`seq_len`, and `hidden_size`, because they often significantly affect the "
"optimal Tiling; however, the `key` is not limited to shape parameters. As "
"long as a parameter change affects configuration selection, it can also be "
"included in the `key`."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:122
msgid "4. 希望参与自动调优的参数不要被提前固定"
msgstr ""
"4\\. Parameters intended for automatic tuning should not be fixed in "
"advance."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:124
msgid "如果希望某个 `tl.constexpr` 参与自动 Tiling 生成，需要同时满足下面三点："
msgstr ""
"If you want a `tl.constexpr` to participate in automatic Tiling generation, "
"the following three conditions must be met simultaneously:"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:126
msgid "它本身必须是 Tiling 参数，也就是会影响每个 block（逻辑核）处理的数据规模或 tile 大小的参数；"
msgstr ""
"It must itself be a Tiling parameter, that is, a parameter that affects the "
"data scale or tile size processed by each block (logical core)."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:127
msgid "不要在 launch 时把它显式传值硬编码；"
msgstr "Do not hardcode it explicitly as a value at launch time."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:128
msgid "不要在 kernel 定义里给它设置默认值。"
msgstr "Do not set a default value for it in the kernel definition."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:130
msgid "例如下面这种写法，`BLOCK_M` 会参与自动调优："
msgstr ""
"For example, in the following code, `BLOCK_M` will participate in automatic "
"tuning:"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:132
msgid ""
"kernel[grid](\n"
"    x,\n"
"    y,\n"
"    out,\n"
"    M,\n"
"    N,\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""
"kernel[grid](\n"
"    x,\n"
"    y,\n"
"    out,\n"
"    M,\n"
"    N,\n"
")\n"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:142
msgid "如果你在 launch 时显式传入："
msgstr "If you explicitly pass in at launch:"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:144
msgid ""
"kernel[grid](\n"
"    x,\n"
"    y,\n"
"    out,\n"
"    M,\n"
"    N,\n"
"    BLOCK_M=128,\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""
"kernel[grid](\n"
"    x,\n"
"    y,\n"
"    out,\n"
"    M,\n"
"    N,\n"
"    BLOCK_M=128,\n"
")\n"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:155
msgid "那这个参数就已经被固定，不再属于自动生成范围。"
msgstr ""
"Then this parameter is already fixed and no longer falls within the scope of"
" automatic generation."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:157
msgid "同样，如果在 kernel 定义中给某个调优参数提供了默认值，例如："
msgstr ""
"Similarly, if a default value is provided for a tuning parameter in the "
"kernel definition, for example:"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:159
msgid ""
"@triton.jit\n"
"def kernel(\n"
"    ...,\n"
"    BLOCK_M: tl.constexpr = 128,\n"
"):\n"
"    ...\n"
msgstr ""
"@triton.jit\n"
"def kernel(\n"
"    ...,\n"
"    BLOCK_M: tl.constexpr = 128,\n"
"):\n"
"    ...\n"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:168
msgid ""
"那么这个参数也不会参与自动调优。对于希望交给框架自动生成和寻优的参数，应该把它保留为“未在 launch 时显式传值、且在 kernel "
"定义中也没有默认值”的 `tl.constexpr`。"
msgstr ""
"Then this parameter will not participate in automatic tuning. For parameters"
" that you want the framework to automatically generate and optimize, you "
"should keep them as `tl.constexpr` that are \"not explicitly assigned a "
"value at launch time and have no default value in the kernel definition.\""

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:170
msgid "5. 如果 Tiling 参数会影响 grid，grid 必须写成 lambda 形式"
msgstr ""
"5\\. If the Tiling parameter affects the grid, the grid must be written in "
"lambda form."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:172
msgid ""
"如果某个 Tiling 参数会影响 grid 大小，那么 grid 不能提前写成固定值或只依赖运行时参数的静态表达式，而必须写成依赖 meta 参数的 "
"`lambda` 形式。这一点与社区 autotune 的要求一致。"
msgstr ""
"If a Tiling parameter affects the grid size, the grid cannot be pre-defined "
"as a fixed value or a static expression that depends only on runtime "
"parameters; instead, it must be written in a `lambda` form that depends on "
"meta parameters. This is consistent with the requirements of the community "
"autotune."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:174
msgid "grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(M, meta[\"BLOCK_M\"]),)\n"
msgstr "grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(M, meta[\"BLOCK_M\"]),)\n"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:178
msgid ""
"原因是 autotune 在评估不同候选配置时，`BLOCK_M` 这类参数的取值会变化；如果 grid "
"不随候选配置一起变化，就无法保证每个候选配置都以正确的发射方式执行。"
msgstr ""
"The reason is that when autotune evaluates different candidate "
"configurations, the values of parameters such as `BLOCK_M` will change; if "
"the grid does not change along with the candidate configurations, there is "
"no guarantee that each candidate configuration will execute with the correct"
" launch method."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:180
msgid "使用注意事项"
msgstr "Usage Notes"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:182
msgid ""
"autotune 的 benchmark 语义与社区一致，会多次执行 kernel。如果 kernel 存在副作用，例如包含原子操作、inplace "
"写入，或会修改输入/输出 buffer 的累积状态，仍然需要通过社区已有的 hook 机制处理。"
msgstr ""
"The benchmark semantics of autotune are consistent with the community, and "
"the kernel will be executed multiple times. If the kernel has side effects, "
"such as containing atomic operations, inplace writes, or modifying the "
"cumulative state of input/output buffers, it still needs to be handled "
"through the existing hook mechanism in the community."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:184
msgid "Triton-Ascend 相比社区 autotune 的扩展"
msgstr "Triton-Ascend's extensions compared to the community autotune."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:186
msgid ""
"社区版 `triton.autotune` 的典型模式是：用户手工提供一组 `triton.Config`，框架做 "
"benchmark，然后缓存最优结果。"
msgstr ""
"The typical pattern for the community edition of `triton.autotune` is: the "
"user manually provides a set of `triton.Config` objects, the framework "
"performs benchmarking, and then caches the optimal result."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:188
msgid "Triton-Ascend 在保持这套接口习惯不变的前提下，主要扩展了下面几件事。"
msgstr ""
"Triton-Ascend primarily extends the following aspects while keeping the "
"interface conventions unchanged."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:190
msgid "1. 支持 `configs=[]` 自动生成候选配置"
msgstr ""
"1\\. Support `configs=[]` to automatically generate candidate "
"configurations."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:192
msgid ""
"这是最核心的扩展。用户不必先手写一组 `triton.Config`，而是可以把 `configs` 留空，让 Ascend backend 根据 "
"kernel DSL 语义和运行时 shape 自动生成候选配置。"
msgstr ""
"This is the most core extension. Users do not need to manually write a set "
"of `triton.Config` in advance; instead, they can leave `configs` empty and "
"let the Ascend backend automatically generate candidate configurations based"
" on the kernel DSL semantics and runtime shapes."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:194
msgid "2. 支持多个 config 的并行编译"
msgstr "2\\. Support parallel compilation of multiple configs."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:196
msgid "当 autotune 需要评估多个候选配置时，Triton-Ascend 默认会并行编译这些候选配置，以缩短首次调优时延。"
msgstr ""
"When autotune needs to evaluate multiple candidate configurations, Triton-"
"Ascend compiles these candidates in parallel by default to reduce the "
"latency of the initial tuning process."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:198
msgid "这一能力默认开启，可通过环境变量 `TRITON_AUTOTUNE_PARALLEL_COMPILE=0` 关闭。"
msgstr ""
"This capability is enabled by default and can be disabled via the "
"environment variable `TRITON_AUTOTUNE_PARALLEL_COMPILE=0`."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:200
msgid "3. 支持使用 profiler 采集 kernel 性能"
msgstr "3\\. Supports using profiler to collect kernel performance."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:202
msgid ""
"Triton-Ascend 支持在 autotune 做 benchmark 时切换性能采集方式：除了默认 benchmark 模式外，还可以使用 "
"profiler 来采集每个候选 config 的 kernel 性能数据，它只关注 kernel 的片上计算时间，对于执行时间较短的 kernel "
"比默认性能采集方式更加精确，但会增加一些耗时。这项能力可通过环境变量 `TRITON_BENCH_METHOD='npu'` 开启。"
msgstr ""
"Triton-Ascend supports switching the performance collection method during "
"autotune benchmarking: in addition to the default benchmark mode, a profiler"
" can be used to collect kernel performance data for each candidate config. "
"It focuses only on the kernel's on-chip computation time, which is more "
"accurate than the default performance collection method for kernels with "
"short execution times, but it adds some overhead. This capability can be "
"enabled via the environment variable `TRITON_BENCH_METHOD='npu'`."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:204
msgid "自动 Tiling 生成能力的范围与行为"
msgstr "Scope and behavior of automatic tiling generation capability"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:206
msgid "前面的第 1 点说明了 Triton-Ascend 支持 `configs=[]` 自动生成候选配置。对这项能力，进行以下几点说明。"
msgstr ""
"The earlier point 1 explains that Triton-Ascend supports `configs=[]` to "
"automatically generate candidate configurations. The following points "
"provide further clarification on this capability."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:208
msgid "1. 自动生成范围聚焦在 Tiling 参数"
msgstr "1\\. The auto-generated scope focuses on the Tiling parameters."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:210
msgid ""
"Ascend 自动生成的重点是 kernel 中与 Tiling 相关的 `tl.constexpr` 参数，也就是影响每个 "
"block（逻辑核）处理的数据规模或 tile 大小的参数。"
msgstr ""
"The focus of Ascend's automatic generation is on the `tl.constexpr` "
"parameters related to Tiling in the kernel, that is, the parameters that "
"affect the data scale processed by each block (logical core) or the tile "
"size."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:212
msgid ""
"这套能力不等价于“自动帮你调所有参数”。像 `num_warps`、`num_stages` 这类编译参数，以及 kernel 的非 Tiling "
"参数，不属于当前自动生成范围。"
msgstr ""
"This capability is not equivalent to \"automatically tuning all parameters "
"for you.\" Compilation parameters such as `num_warps` and `num_stages`, as "
"well as non-Tiling parameters of the kernel, are not within the current "
"scope of automatic generation."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:214
msgid "2. 候选配置会带上 Ascend 硬件约束"
msgstr "2\\. Candidate configurations will carry Ascend Hardware constraints."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:216
msgid ""
"Ascend backend 在生成候选时，会结合 NPU 的片上存储容量、对齐约束、核数利用等边界做筛选，而不是单纯枚举一批配置再盲目 "
"benchmark。"
msgstr ""
"When generating candidates, the Ascend backend filters them based on "
"constraints such as the NPU's on-chip storage capacity, alignment "
"requirements, and core utilization, rather than simply enumerating a batch "
"of configurations and then blindly benchmarking them."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:218
msgid "3. 自动 Tiling 模式的目标是方便给出“性能不错”的配置"
msgstr ""
"3\\. The goal of the automatic tiling mode is to conveniently provide a "
"configuration with \"decent performance.\""

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:220
msgid "为了权衡寻优时间和寻优效果，当前自动 Tiling 会对生成配置数量做大量剪枝，因此并不保证自动生成结果一定能达到手工极致调优的性能上限。"
msgstr ""
"To balance optimization time and optimization effectiveness, the current "
"automatic Tiling performs extensive pruning on the number of generated "
"configurations, so it does not guarantee that the automatically generated "
"results will necessarily reach the performance upper limit of manual extreme"
" tuning."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:222
msgid "这项能力的目标，是在尽量降低用户使用门槛和寻优成本的前提下，方便地给用户提供一个性能还不错的 Tiling 配置。"
msgstr ""
"The goal of this capability is to conveniently provide users with a Tiling "
"configuration that offers decent performance, while minimizing the barrier "
"to entry and the cost of optimization for users."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:224
msgid "4. 自动 Tiling 生成失败时需要用户手写 `triton.Config`"
msgstr ""
"4\\. When automatic tiling generation fails, users need to manually write "
"`triton.Config`."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:226
msgid ""
"如果自动 Tiling 模式无法生成任何可用候选配置，这时需要用户改为手写 `triton.Config`。同时也建议对这类场景提 issue，帮助 "
"Triton-Ascend 后续补齐解析和自动生成能力。"
msgstr ""
"If the automatic Tiling mode cannot generate any usable candidate "
"configurations, the user needs to switch to manually writing "
"`triton.Config`. It is also recommended to file an issue for such scenarios "
"to help Triton-Ascend improve its parsing and automatic generation "
"capabilities in the future."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:228
msgid "手写 `triton.Config` 模式"
msgstr "Handwritten `triton.Config` pattern"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:230
msgid ""
"如果自动 Tiling 模式生成失败，或生成的 Tiling 性能未达到预期，直接回到社区标准写法即可。Triton-Ascend "
"对这部分语义保持兼容："
msgstr ""
"If automatic Tiling mode generation fails, or the generated Tiling "
"performance does not meet expectations, simply revert to the community "
"standard implementation. Triton-Ascend maintains compatibility with this "
"part of the semantics."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:232
msgid ""
"@triton.autotune(\n"
"    configs=[\n"
"        triton.Config({\"BLOCK_M\": 128, \"BLOCK_N\": 128}),\n"
"        triton.Config({\"BLOCK_M\": 64, \"BLOCK_N\": 256}),\n"
"    ],\n"
"    key=[\"M\", \"N\"],\n"
")\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def kernel(...):\n"
"    ...\n"
msgstr ""
"@triton.autotune(\n"
"    configs=[\n"
"        triton.Config({\"BLOCK_M\": 128, \"BLOCK_N\": 128}),\n"
"        triton.Config({\"BLOCK_M\": 64, \"BLOCK_N\": 256}),\n"
"    ],\n"
"    key=[\"M\", \"N\"],\n"
")\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def kernel(...):\n"
"    ...\n"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:245
msgid "这一模式下："
msgstr "In this mode:"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:247
msgid "配置由用户手工提供；"
msgstr "Configuration is manually provided by the user;"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:248
msgid "框架负责 benchmark、选择最优配置和缓存复用；"
msgstr ""
"The framework is responsible for benchmarking, selecting the optimal "
"configuration, and cache reuse."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:249
msgid "使用习惯与社区 autotune 保持一致。"
msgstr "Usage habits remain consistent with the community autotune."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:251
msgid "查看调优日志"
msgstr "View tuning logs"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:253
msgid ""
"设置 "
"`TRITON_PRINT_AUTOTUNING=1`，可查看调优日志。实际完成测速后，会打印调优耗时、最佳配置和各个成功配置的测速结果。以下为示意输出（`...`"
" 表示省略的配置参数）："
msgstr "View tuning logs"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:255
msgid ""
"Triton autotuning for function kernel finished after 0.12s; best config selected: BLOCK_M: 128, BLOCK_N: 128, ...;\n"
"Triton autotuning benchmark results for function kernel:\n"
"  config=BLOCK_M: 128, BLOCK_N: 128, ...; p50=0.0100 ms, p20=0.0090 ms, p80=0.0110 ms [selected]\n"
"  config=BLOCK_M: 64, BLOCK_N: 256, ...; p50=0.0140 ms, p20=0.0130 ms, p80=0.0150 ms\n"
msgstr ""
"Triton autotuning for function kernel finished after 0.12s; best config selected: BLOCK_M: 128, BLOCK_N: 128, ...;\n"
"Triton autotuning benchmark results for function kernel:\n"
"  config=BLOCK_M: 128, BLOCK_N: 128, ...; p50=0.0100 ms, p20=0.0090 ms, p80=0.0110 ms [selected]\n"
"  config=BLOCK_M: 64, BLOCK_N: 256, ...; p50=0.0140 ms, p20=0.0130 ms, p80=0.0150 ms\n"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:262
msgid ""
"`[selected]` 标记被选中的最佳配置。`p50`、`p20`、`p80` 分别为第 50、20、80 "
"百分位耗时，单位为毫秒；若测速返回平均耗时，则显示 `mean=... ms`。"
msgstr ""
"The `[selected]` marker indicates the best configuration selected. `p50`, "
"`p20`, and `p80` represent the 50th, 20th, and 80th percentile latencies in "
"milliseconds, respectively. If the benchmark returns the average latency, "
"`mean=... ms` is displayed."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:264
msgid ""
"用户配置（`configs`，包括通过 `hints` "
"展开的配置）发生失败，或调优因异常中断时，会打印相应配置的状态和原因。以下分别为编译失败和调优中断的示意输出："
msgstr ""
"When user configurations (`configs`, including configurations expanded "
"through `hints`) fail, or tuning is interrupted by an exception, the status "
"and reason for each configuration will be printed. The following shows "
"sample outputs for compilation failure and tuning interruption, "
"respectively:"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:266
msgid ""
"Triton autotuning: config=BLOCK_M: 128, BLOCK_N: 128, ...; compile_failed; reason=CompileTimeAssertionFailure: <错误信息>\n"
"Triton autotuning: config=BLOCK_M: 64, BLOCK_N: 256, ...; not_evaluated; reason=No benchmark result was produced. Autotuning interrupted: RuntimeError: <错误信息>\n"
msgstr ""
"Triton autotuning: config=BLOCK_M: 128, BLOCK_N: 128, ...; compile_failed; reason=CompileTimeAssertionFailure: <error message>\n"
"Triton autotuning: config=BLOCK_M: 64, BLOCK_N: 256, ...; not_evaluated; reason=No benchmark result was produced. Autotuning interrupted: RuntimeError: <error message>\n"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:271
msgid ""
"其中，`compile_failed` 表示编译失败，`not_evaluated` 表示配置尚未完成评估，`reason` 给出失败或中断原因。"
msgstr ""
"Here, `compile_failed` indicates a compilation failure, `not_evaluated` "
"indicates that the configuration has not been evaluated yet, and `reason` "
"provides the failure or interruption reason."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:273
msgid "进阶用法：自动 Tiling 与其他参数联合调优"
msgstr ""
"Advanced Usage: Joint Tuning of Automatic Tiling with Other Parameters"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:275
msgid ""
"以下内容属于进阶用法，只有当用户希望在自动 Tiling 模式下，继续联合调优 kernel 的非 Tiling 参数或编译参数时，再考虑使用。"
msgstr ""
"The following content pertains to advanced usage and should only be "
"considered when users wish to continue jointly tuning non-Tiling parameters "
"or compilation parameters of the kernel in automatic Tiling mode."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:277
msgid "1. 社区 autotune：手工枚举全部调优参数"
msgstr "1\\. Community autotune: manually enumerate all tuning parameters"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:279
msgid "社区标准写法是由用户手工枚举所有候选配置："
msgstr ""
"The community standard approach is for users to manually enumerate all "
"candidate configurations:"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:281
msgid ""
"@triton.autotune(\n"
"    configs=[\n"
"        triton.Config(\n"
"            {\n"
"                \"BLOCK_M\": BM,\n"
"                \"BLOCK_N\": BN,\n"
"                \"BLOCK_K\": BK,\n"
"                \"GROUP_SIZE_M\": GS,\n"
"            },\n"
"            num_warps=num_warps,\n"
"        )\n"
"        for BM in [16, 32, 64]\n"
"        for BN in [16, 32, 64]\n"
"        for BK in [16, 32, 64]\n"
"        for GS in [1, 2, 4, 8]\n"
"        for num_warps in [1, 2, 4, 8]\n"
"    ],\n"
"    key=[\"M\", \"N\", \"K\"],\n"
")\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def matmul_kernel(a, b, M, N, K, BLOCK_M, BLOCK_N, BLOCK_K, GROUP_SIZE_M):\n"
"    ...\n"
msgstr ""
"@triton.autotune(\n"
"    configs=[\n"
"        triton.Config(\n"
"            {\n"
"                \"BLOCK_M\": BM,\n"
"                \"BLOCK_N\": BN,\n"
"                \"BLOCK_K\": BK,\n"
"                \"GROUP_SIZE_M\": GS,\n"
"            },\n"
"            num_warps=num_warps,\n"
"        )\n"
"        for BM in [16, 32, 64]\n"
"        for BN in [16, 32, 64]\n"
"        for BK in [16, 32, 64]\n"
"        for GS in [1, 2, 4, 8]\n"
"        for num_warps in [1, 2, 4, 8]\n"
"    ],\n"
"    key=[\"M\", \"N\", \"K\"],\n"
")\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def matmul_kernel(a, b, M, N, K, BLOCK_M, BLOCK_N, BLOCK_K, GROUP_SIZE_M):\n"
"    ...\n"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:306
msgid "2. Triton-Ascend：手工枚举 Tiling 参数和 Ascend 编译参数"
msgstr ""
"2\\. Triton-Ascend: Manually enumerate Tiling parameters and Ascend "
"compilation parameters"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:308
msgid "在 Triton-Ascend 中，如果希望继续走手工枚举模式，也可以把 Ascend 侧参数一起放进手工配置空间："
msgstr ""
"In Triton-Ascend, if you wish to continue using the manual enumeration mode,"
" you can also include the Ascend-side parameters in the manual configuration"
" space."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:310
msgid ""
"@triton.autotune(\n"
"    configs=[\n"
"        triton.Config(\n"
"            {\n"
"                \"BLOCK_M\": BM,\n"
"                \"BLOCK_N\": BN,\n"
"                \"BLOCK_K\": BK,\n"
"                \"GROUP_SIZE_M\": GS,\n"
"                \"multibuffer\": MS,\n"
"            }\n"
"        )\n"
"        for BM in [16, 32, 64]\n"
"        for BN in [16, 32, 64]\n"
"        for BK in [16, 32, 64]\n"
"        for GS in [1, 2, 4, 8]\n"
"        for MS in [False, True]\n"
"    ],\n"
"    key=[\"M\", \"N\", \"K\"],\n"
")\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def matmul_kernel(a, b, M, N, K, BLOCK_M, BLOCK_N, BLOCK_K, GROUP_SIZE_M):\n"
"    ...\n"
msgstr ""
"@triton.autotune(\n"
"    configs=[\n"
"        triton.Config(\n"
"            {\n"
"                \"BLOCK_M\": BM,\n"
"                \"BLOCK_N\": BN,\n"
"                \"BLOCK_K\": BK,\n"
"                \"GROUP_SIZE_M\": GS,\n"
"                \"multibuffer\": MS,\n"
"            }\n"
"        )\n"
"        for BM in [16, 32, 64]\n"
"        for BN in [16, 32, 64]\n"
"        for BK in [16, 32, 64]\n"
"        for GS in [1, 2, 4, 8]\n"
"        for MS in [False, True]\n"
"    ],\n"
"    key=[\"M\", \"N\", \"K\"],\n"
")\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def matmul_kernel(a, b, M, N, K, BLOCK_M, BLOCK_N, BLOCK_K, GROUP_SIZE_M):\n"
"    ...\n"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:335
msgid "3. Triton-Ascend：自动生成 Tiling，同时联合调优其他参数"
msgstr ""
"3\\. Triton-Ascend: Automatically generates Tiling while jointly tuning "
"other parameters."

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:337
msgid ""
"如果希望 Tiling 参数继续由 `configs=[]` 自动生成，但又希望同时调优其他非 Tiling 参数或编译参数，可以把这些额外搜索维度通过"
" `hints` 传入："
msgstr ""
"If you want the Tiling parameters to continue being automatically generated "
"by `configs=[]`, but also want to tune other non-Tiling parameters or "
"compilation parameters at the same time, you can pass these additional "
"search dimensions through `hints`:"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:339
msgid ""
"@triton.autotune(\n"
"    configs=[],\n"
"    key=[\"M\", \"N\", \"K\"],\n"
"    hints={\n"
"        \"GROUP_SIZE_M\": [1, 2, 4, 8],\n"
"        \"multibuffer\": [False, True],\n"
"    },\n"
")\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def matmul_kernel(a, b, M, N, K, BLOCK_M, BLOCK_N, BLOCK_K, GROUP_SIZE_M):\n"
"    ...\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(M, meta[\"BLOCK_M\"]) * meta[\"GROUP_SIZE_M\"], triton.cdiv(N, meta[\"BLOCK_N\"]))\n"
"matmul_kernel[grid](a, b, M, N, K)\n"
msgstr ""
"@triton.autotune(\n"
"    configs=[],\n"
"    key=[\"M\", \"N\", \"K\"],\n"
"    hints={\n"
"        \"GROUP_SIZE_M\": [1, 2, 4, 8],\n"
"        \"multibuffer\": [False, True],\n"
"    },\n"
")\n"
"@triton.jit\n"
"def matmul_kernel(a, b, M, N, K, BLOCK_M, BLOCK_N, BLOCK_K, GROUP_SIZE_M):\n"
"    ...\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(M, meta[\"BLOCK_M\"]) * meta[\"GROUP_SIZE_M\"], triton.cdiv(N, meta[\"BLOCK_N\"]))\n"
"matmul_kernel[grid](a, b, M, N, K)\n"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:357
msgid "这种方式的含义是："
msgstr "The meaning of this approach is:"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:359
msgid "Tiling 相关参数仍然由 Triton-Ascend 自动生成；"
msgstr ""
"Tiling-related parameters are still automatically generated by Triton-"
"Ascend;"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:360
msgid ""
"非 Tiling 参数或编译参数（如 `GROUP_SIZE_M` 和 `multibuffer`）由用户通过 `hints` 显式给出候选集合；"
msgstr ""
"Non-Tiling parameters or compilation parameters (such as `GROUP_SIZE_M` and "
"`multibuffer`) are explicitly provided by the user as candidate sets via "
"`hints`;"

#: ../../zh/autotune_guide.md:361
msgid "autotune 会对两部分组合后的配置空间做评估。"
msgstr ""
"autotune will evaluate the configuration space after combining the two "
"parts."

